Subject: Re: eXcursion problem
Date: 1997/03/14
Message-ID: <33296035.7183@alf.dec.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 225479783
References: <5gap22$261@clarion.carno.net.au>
Organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec,comp.windows.x,comp.sys.vms,comp.unix.osf.osf1


Bill Alford wrote:
> 
> I have a user having difficulties with eXcursion V2 on a PC running
> Windows 95. When using Matlab the menu items and buttons text is coming out
> in some Asian font. This only happens with Matlab. Matlab running on the
> host DEC OSF/1 machine doesn't exhibit this problem. Everything else
> appears to run OK with eXcursion. Does anybody have a fix for this?
> 

Asian, or line drawing?  It may be for example that the app is
wildcarding a  font and picking up a DECtech font instead of an iso8859
font.  Is Matlab using its own fonts?  Or *attempting* to use its own
fonts?  It might be that Matlab is expecting to find some of its own
fonts and when they are not there it settles for some non-optimal
alternative. 
-- 
